From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 21:26:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 223/225] arm64: dts: ums512: drop idle-injection cooling maps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With real A75 voltage scaling, cpufreq cooling cuts power ~f*V^2
per step and regulates sustained all-core load (openssl speed
-multi 8) at 68-71C against the 70C passive trips on its own —
idle injection never needed. Under the old pinned-voltage bypass
the same load ran away toward critical, which is why the idle
injectors were added. Remove the cooling maps; keep the per-cpu
thermal-idle nodes so the injectors stay available as an easy
backstop if a future config needs them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
